    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21560" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illūcĕo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inl-</span></b> ), ēre,
			v. n.
		in-luceo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to shine in</i> or <i>on</i>, <i>to light up</i>, <i>illuminate</i>,
				<i>give light</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pix atra tuo capiti illuceat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt. 3, 4, 65</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tota domus tua veri fulgore solis illuceat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Psa. 118</span></i>
			, Serm. 19, 39.</div>
